{{define "progress"}}
<h1>How far it goes</h1>

<p>Three questions, three sources, three denominators. They are not combined
into one score, because a single number over all three would mean nothing.</p>

{{template "pagechart" .Lint}}

<h2>Which population this measures</h2>

<p>Only one population here is written by people outside this project, and only
that one measures the promise. The manifest marks it, and the marking is
carried onto this page rather than dropped.</p>

<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Origin</th><th>Configs</th><th>Clean</th><th>Blocked</th><th>Reads as</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {{range .Progress.Populations}}<tr>
    <td>{{.Origin}}</td><td>{{.Configs}}</td><td>{{.Clean}}</td><td>{{.Blocked}}</td>
    <td>{{if .IsRate}}<strong>a rate</strong>{{else}}a ranking{{end}}</td>
  </tr>{{end}}
  </tbody>
</table>

<p>A ranking orders work. A rate says how often a configuration nobody here
wrote gets through. Adding the three together produces a flattering figure
carried by fixtures written to pass, so the headline uses the rate population
alone.</p>

<h2>What to build next</h2>

<p>Ranked by how many configurations each missing type blocks, from
<code>unadmitted_demand</code>. {{.Progress.TotalDemand}} AWS types are on the
full list. A further {{.Progress.OtherProvider}} belong to other providers and
are left out, because this project is AWS only and no work here admits
them.</p>

<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Configs blocked</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {{range .Progress.Demand}}<tr><td><code>{{.Type}}</code></td><td>{{.Configs}}</td></tr>{{end}}
  </tbody>
</table>

{{template "pagechart" .Crossing}}

<p>Passing lint and surviving a run are different claims. The first says a
configuration is admissible. The second says an estate stood up, lost its state
file, and replanned empty. <a href="estates.html">Every estate</a> lists where
each one stopped.</p>

{{template "pagechart" .IAM}}

<p>This axis is not a measure of this project. It is AWS's own coverage of the
condition key per-resource scoping depends on.
<a href="governance.html">Scoping a role</a> has the full roster.</p>

<h2>Where these numbers come from</h2>

<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Chart</th><th>Artifact</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Passes live-check</td><td><code>live/corpus-refusals.json</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td>Survives a real run</td><td><code>live/corpus-crossing-manifest.json</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td>IAM can scope it</td><td><code>live/iam-reference.json</code></td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<p>Every figure on this page is rendered from a committed artifact at build
time. None is typed by hand. A wrong number here means a stale artifact, and
regenerating it fixes the page.</p>
{{end}}

{{define "pagechart"}}
<figure class="chart" id="chart-{{.ID}}">
  <figcaption>
    <strong>{{.Title}}</strong>
    <span class="denominator">{{.Denominator}}</span>
  </figcaption>
  <div class="bars">
    {{range .Bars}}
    <div class="bar-row{{if .Muted}} bar-muted{{end}}">
      <span class="bar-label">{{.Label}}</span>
      {{if .Unmeasured}}
      <span class="bar-unmeasured">{{.Unmeasured}}</span>
      <span class="bar-value"></span>
      {{else}}
      <span class="bar-track"><span class="bar-fill" style="width:{{printf "%.1f" .Percent}}%"></span></span>
      <span class="bar-value">{{.Value}}</span>
      {{end}}
    </div>
    {{end}}
  </div>
</figure>
{{end}}
